Verse 1:
[G]All people [Em]that [Bm]on [Em]earth [D]do [G]dwell, Sing to the [D]Lord [Em]with [C]cheerful [D]voice;
[Em]Him [D/F#]serve [G]with [D]mirth, [G/B]His [C]praise [D7/A]forth [G]tell, Come ye [Em]before [Am]Him [Bm]and [D]rejoice.

Verse 2:
[G]Know [D]that [Bm]the [D]Lord [G]is [D]God [C]indeed;
[G]without [Bm]our [D]aid [G]he did [Em]us [G]make;
[Em]we [G]are his [D7/A]folk, [G]he [Em]doth [Am]us [D]feed,
[Em]and [G]for his [D7/A]sheep [G]he [Em]doth [Am]us [D]take.

Verse 3:
[G]O enter [Em]then [G]his gates [Em]with [G]praise;
[G]approach [Bm]with [D]joy [G]his courts [Em]unto;
[Em]praise, [G]laud, and [D7/A]bless [G]his [Em]name [Am]always,
[Em]for [G]it is [D7/A]seemly [Em]so [Am]to [D]do.

Verse 4:
[G]For [D]why! [Bm]the [D]Lord [G]our God [Em]is [G]good;
[G]his [D]mercy is [G]forever sure;
[Em]his [D/F#]truth at [C]all [G]times [Em]firmly [D]stood,
[Em]and [G]shall from [D7/A]age [G]to [Em]age [Am]endure.
